00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.210
- Yeah yeah thank you.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:49.184
And I see you Kirby.

00:14:49.184 --> 00:14:51.653
Hi (laughs) (mumbles).

00:14:51.653 --> 00:14:54.750
To get onto the question about friar

00:14:55.875 --> 00:14:59.097
and kind of friar intellectual
botanical knowledge, right?

00:14:59.097 --> 00:15:02.470
And botanical production, I
think in Philippine history,

00:15:02.470 --> 00:15:07.470
one of the best study friars
who is up to kind of natural

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.720
at this work is Francisco Manuel Blanco.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.520
We studied his Florida Filipinos

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:14.810
which was written and published in 1837

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.698
sort of up and down as
one of the first texts

00:15:17.698 --> 00:15:19.740
of Philippine botany.

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:21.367
And this is being done
both in the social sciences

00:15:21.367 --> 00:15:22.770
and in sciences as well

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.730
I mean, we're still really
investigating his work.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:28.133
And I think it's an
important text, no doubt

00:15:28.133 --> 00:15:31.040
but what I find really
fascinating in the archives

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.160
is at least by the 19th century

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:37.380
the Spanish state is really
trying to separate itself

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:39.740
from the work of the Spanish friars

00:15:39.740 --> 00:15:41.140
and the work that's being done

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.440
by secular officials in the Spanish state.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.230
I kind of call this more of
like a scientific state craft

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.260
if you will.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:49.960
Other scholars have looked
at how late Spanish empire

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:53.920
starts to double down and really
show its intellectual chops

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.900
to sort of the new Imperial world

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.790
this is happening as well in
the Philippines with botany.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.300
And so at some point there
were some great letters

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:03.561
in Madrid covering this

00:16:03.561 --> 00:16:06.460
different metropolitan
centers are interested

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.698
in the botany that's going
on in the Philippines.

00:16:09.698 --> 00:16:11.970
They're asking for texts that are coming

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.150
and being produced on the Philippines.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:17.416
And some of them ask for
Lancos Florida Filipinas

00:16:17.416 --> 00:16:19.987
the Spanish state actually
comes in and says,

00:16:19.987 --> 00:16:21.730
"Yeah, it's good."

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:23.430
But that was an Augustinian publication

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.163
and now look at the
synopsis, check this out.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.690
I mean, this is my
hilarious summarizing of it

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:32.340
but I think that's a really
important moment, right?

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.550
This distinction that's starting to happen

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.090
between sort of friar
science and the science

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:39.430
in the secular state.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.780
And what it's supposed to be doing

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:42.310
for positioning the Spanish empire

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.200
in a very different way in botany

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.933
than it had been in the first
1/2 of the 19th century.

00:16:48.574 --> 00:16:50.463
There's a much more money
going into botany at the end

00:16:50.463 --> 00:16:52.350
of the 19th century than we've
really seen in other parts

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.493
of the 19th century.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:57.150
When it comes to Malaysia or Malesia

00:16:57.150 --> 00:16:58.850
depending on how you pronounce it.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:02.510
I think it's a really important
kind of floristic region

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:04.750
to take note of, because what we're seeing

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.360
at least in this time period
around the turn of the century

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:11.560
is that botanists are
creating a region of their own

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:13.830
that they believe is
prescribed by plant life.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:16.279
Really the movement of
particular plant genera

00:17:16.279 --> 00:17:18.563
across the different domains.

00:17:18.563 --> 00:17:21.140
What they're acknowledging
is that this plant genera is

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.220
really a vast (mumbles) terrains

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:26.550
so it's no longer just
about Philippine flora

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.100
versus Duchies, in these flora versus that

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:32.700
in British Malaya you're
seeing what the flora is

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.320
across these domains.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.750
And so Malaysia as a region
starts to gain a lot of credence

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:41.020
and salience among these botanists.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.100
Why do I find this
interesting well, I'm a child

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:46.550
of area studies I've been
in Southeast Asian studies

00:17:47.531 --> 00:17:48.770
until I was 18 I love the field

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:50.350
And for all of us who were trained

00:17:50.350 --> 00:17:51.450
in Southeast Asian studies

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:54.150
we know that the apogee is
really around world war II.

00:17:55.004 --> 00:17:56.318
(person clears throat)

00:17:56.318 --> 00:17:59.120
To film and gain social
scientific prominence

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.530
as a result of world war II

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:02.330
and eventually cold war politicking.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:06.250
I'd like to push that a
little bit further back

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.139
and if you look at the domain of science,

00:18:09.139 --> 00:18:10.910
specifically botany region
making was happening

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:12.333
well before world war II.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:15.080
And again, I think a
lot of these botanists

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:16.530
are sort of seeing themselves

00:18:17.856 --> 00:18:19.900
as standing outside of
politics and politicking.

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.510
But when you look at again,
the sort of interim period

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.160
configuration that's
happening at the time,

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.060
they're very much part of it

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:28.780
but they're using sort of
botany as this explanation

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:31.660
for why and sort of reach
and making will make sense.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:34.370
And so Malaysia as a place,
really takes part in that

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:37.460
and it's still considered
a floristic sub-region

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.870
of the Indo-Malayan biogeographic zone.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:43.230
So there are presently
botanists and scientists

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.420
within Southeast Asia who are contributing

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:47.247
to the flora Malaysiana catalog,

00:18:47.247 --> 00:18:51.110
and really still seeing
it as a concrete place

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.260
where we can map forum.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.880
- [Erik] Thanks Kat this
is really fascinating

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.510
and someday I'd love to ask
you much deeper questions

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:05.470
about Malaysia, but I wanted
to turn to another part

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.221
