that measurement of a plant

00:40:42.790 --> 00:40:45.560
or even the scale of a plant can change

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:47.290
depending on the discourse.

00:40:47.290 --> 00:40:49.090
And so if you look back to chapter three,

00:40:49.090 --> 00:40:51.013
you think back to the sampaguita

00:40:51.013 --> 00:40:53.680
and you think about measurement
and growing space, right?

00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:56.130
And how that growing
space actually enlarges

00:40:56.130 --> 00:40:58.793
depending on sort of the imagination.

00:40:58.793 --> 00:41:01.130
And then, I say imagination

00:41:01.130 --> 00:41:04.380
but I mean sort of how
intellectuals at the time

00:41:04.380 --> 00:41:06.050
are both grounding their imagination

00:41:06.050 --> 00:41:08.490
in scientific texts but also allowing

00:41:08.490 --> 00:41:09.770
for a national imagination

00:41:09.770 --> 00:41:14.130
to really enlarge the growing
expense of the sampaguita.

00:41:14.130 --> 00:41:15.380
And then we have sort of measurement

00:41:15.380 --> 00:41:17.010
turned on its head, right?

00:41:17.010 --> 00:41:19.530
We actually are inverting
sort of the land,

00:41:19.530 --> 00:41:22.000
the norms of measurement
and plant description

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:25.340
and allowing it to become
sort of allowing the plant

00:41:25.340 --> 00:41:28.570
to become much more encompassing
of the white archipelago.

00:41:28.570 --> 00:41:30.710
And that's a really exciting part, right?

00:41:30.710 --> 00:41:32.160
How does the sampaguita itself

00:41:32.160 --> 00:41:35.220
sort of push these Lunean norms?

00:41:35.220 --> 00:41:36.643
So really thank you for bringing that up

