00:43:33.496 --> 00:43:35.090
In terms of internationalizing botany

00:43:35.090 --> 00:43:37.090
that I can talk about
a little bit more about

00:43:37.090 --> 00:43:38.070
and geographic bias.

00:43:38.070 --> 00:43:39.820
I actually think geographic
bias is happening

00:43:39.820 --> 00:43:42.217
on different scales in the dissertation

00:43:42.217 --> 00:43:44.470
and in how we look at this history, right?

00:43:44.470 --> 00:43:47.150
Even if botany is
internationalizing at the time

00:43:47.150 --> 00:43:50.340
the biggest movers and shakers of botany

00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:53.487
are all sort of Imperial
metropolitan centers.

00:43:53.487 --> 00:43:55.860
And so the notion of the
international is really

00:43:55.860 --> 00:44:00.547
only kind of geographically
limited to Europe at the time.

00:44:00.547 --> 00:44:03.080
And this sort of extends to the
United States at some point,

00:44:03.080 --> 00:44:05.320
but it's pretty limited.

00:44:05.320 --> 00:44:07.590
I think when we're thinking
about Philippine flora as well

00:44:07.590 --> 00:44:10.133
the geographic biases is mostly in Duzon

00:44:10.133 --> 00:44:12.250
and certainly Manila.

00:44:12.250 --> 00:44:15.670
These are very well studied
locations for botany

00:44:15.670 --> 00:44:18.069
up until sort of the early 20th century.

00:44:18.069 --> 00:44:21.050
There are other investigations
that are happening

00:44:21.050 --> 00:44:23.729
I mean, there's this extension
penetration of Mindenal.

00:44:23.729 --> 00:44:26.870
It starts around the
mid 19th century as well

00:44:26.870 --> 00:44:29.260
and it's flora is getting
sort of considered

00:44:29.260 --> 00:44:32.490
in this colonial catalog that's building.

00:44:32.490 --> 00:44:34.380
But I would even argue
that again, much of this

00:44:34.380 --> 00:44:37.600
colonial catalog is
really sort of situated

00:44:37.600 --> 00:44:40.960
in the colonial capital, radiates outward,

00:44:40.960 --> 00:44:43.030
and then only kind of decades later

00:44:43.030 --> 00:44:45.190
is it incorporating other zones.

00:44:45.190 --> 00:44:48.050
And so you asked, about
Cordilleran peoples

00:44:48.050 --> 00:44:50.990
or peoples in Mindanao, and
whether plant life there

00:44:50.990 --> 00:44:53.730
is sort of getting considered, right?

00:44:53.730 --> 00:44:55.360
Or if it's being considered invasive

00:44:55.360 --> 00:44:57.020
or if there's a particular rhetoric.

00:44:57.020 --> 00:44:59.300
I actually think during this
late Spanish colonial period

00:44:59.300 --> 00:45:01.000
not enough is really known

00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:03.950
but what is known is
the commercial potential

00:45:03.950 --> 00:45:06.610
of these locations,
particularly the timber

00:45:06.610 --> 00:45:08.610
that's coming out of Mindanao.

00:45:08.610 --> 00:45:10.700
And that makes it become a much more

00:45:10.700 --> 00:45:13.280
lucrative place for investigation.

00:45:13.280 --> 00:45:16.250
But I would say in terms of
taxonomic botany, absolutely

00:45:16.250 --> 00:45:19.883
there is still kind of
this geographic bias

00:45:19.883 --> 00:45:21.830
up through kind of the earliest decades

00:45:21.830 --> 00:45:23.860
of the US colonial period.

00:45:23.860 --> 00:45:26.470
And then that has again,
lead into questions about

00:45:26.470 --> 00:45:28.840
well what are we considering
as part of regional botany

00:45:28.840 --> 00:45:30.530
as it's developing at the time?

00:45:30.530 --> 00:45:34.320
What's being constituted as
participating in this creation

00:45:34.320 --> 00:45:35.800
of the regional zone

00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:38.710
and how are those
limitations being expressed?

00:45:38.710 --> 00:45:41.290
And that guys, it ties
back into Al's question,

00:45:41.290 --> 00:45:42.440
where does measurement then

00:45:42.440 --> 00:45:44.708
become a little bit more elastic?

00:45:44.708 --> 00:45:47.800
Geographical space
become much more elastic

00:45:47.800 --> 00:45:49.793
to meet these intellectual ends.

